WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.011
01 · Start with a workshop
Open the original NES workshop. Your own ROMs are not needed for this exercise.

00:00:10.018 --> 00:00:24.027
02 · Assemble a sprite
Graphics & fonts → Assemble tiles. Fit enlarges the preview without resizing the stored image.

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:36.036
03 · Make one small change
Focus Editing, press Right Arrow, then Space. Compare the edited pixel with Original.

00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:48.052
04 · Undo and redo
Undo restores the original stroke. Redo brings the staged edit back.

00:00:48.057 --> 00:01:06.066
05 · Review and create a build
Review asset changes, then Create asset build. The original file stays unchanged.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:18.078
06 · Select and load your build
Playtest build selects the recorded output. Load game uses the included NES engine.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:30.091
07 · Play and pause
This original drawing program repeats the edited tile. Pause before saving a state.

00:01:30.097 --> 00:01:48.105
08 · Save and load a state
Save state, then Load state. States belong to the exact build and engine setup.

00:01:48.109 --> 00:02:10.119
09 · Export a verified patch
Choose the original and your build. Create a BPS patch, then download it.

00:02:10.123 --> 00:02:26.137
10 · Reopen the project
Close the project with Choose a project. Open it again: the source and build remain available.

00:02:26.143 --> 00:02:44.154
11 · Recover a saved draft
Make another small edit on the original. Wait for Saved, then reload: the draft is still there.

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:52.161
12 · Try it yourself
A saved draft is not a new build. Follow the beginner checklist and note anything unclear.

